// logos.std.prelude — the implicit OS-touching surface on top of mem.
//
// Currently identical to mem.prelude in items (Rust's std prelude adds
// nothing of its own beyond core/alloc). The file exists so the layered
// structure stays uniform: a consumer selecting `logos.std.prelude` gets
// the full transitive surface. See docs/core-port/prelude-design.md.
#![no_implicit_prelude]
package logos.std.prelude;

pub use logos.mem.prelude;
// (No std-only additions at this time.)
